ccurate but misleading frames."}, {"id": "6326f176-0dfb-4d36-9c06-97693c455f23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Uncertainty and limits", "children": [{"id": "88164492-e721-444e-97ea-9aeccc6e5a21", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribution of uncertainty"}, {"id": "ac595631-326b-4d2d-a979-99a229429dd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Developing stories"}, {"id": "f33f7f6b-7440-486e-b862-cf50c7fb0eab", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections risk"}, {"id": "41de8280-a27b-4ff2-a51a-91495e075eb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding overclaiming"}], "description": "Students learn to say what is known, unknown, contested, or still developing."}]}, {"id": "6e0b3b58-6bd4-4b51-a817-979db7df53b9", "type": "topic", "title": "Independence and Conflicts of Interest", "description": "Clarifies how journalists protect independence from political, financial, personal, source, and platform pressures.", "children": [{"id": "f8e35a44-43b7-42bc-8ac7-bc7c6e75f9cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Personal conflicts", "children": [{"id": "e292bd9b-df75-4c0c-9337-a58bd97958ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Family ties"}, {"id": "22b8b3e0-22db-4cc7-9885-986b2af08a07", "type": "concept", "title": "Political activity"}, {"id": "0857b0b7-a4ae-455d-9058-1962d9c679f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Gifts and favors"}, {"id": "9449f7c2-6665-4cfb-b8aa-d479fd7fe6de", "type": "concept", "title": "Outside employment"}], "description": "Students identify relationships and commitments that can compromise trust or judgment."}, {"id": "56e42b8a-0e9c-4057-8e5e-d142b2c771eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutional pressures", "children": [{"id": "1aec970f-3fb7-490b-92bc-54d26020b1ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Sponsored content"}, {"id": "ba600341-9daa-4b66-9028-04c444a61e3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Advertiser influence"}, {"id": "4620b9d1-5ea0-417b-9a11-d4aa4d813d5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Click pressure"}, {"id": "d67fbe59-f934-4a40-9241-474284147e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Foundation funding"}], "description": "Newsroom ethics also involves owners, advertisers, funders, platforms, and audience incentives."}, {"id": "dc450e51-909e-49c4-b6d1-354e8e395937", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Independence practices", "children": [{"id": "60eddc68-ae61-4eaf-a3ea-67d3db5d7b1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosure"}, {"id": "b946393a-6911-41dc-a508-9f77f0f7f804", "type": "concept", "title": "Recusal"}, {"id": "4ced168f-75d2-4b92-97ac-dcdec9ae5b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Source boundaries"}, {"id": "45b90939-19d9-42d8-be5f-7f0ac5fe71a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media conduct"}], "description": "Clear boundaries help journalists maintain both actual and perceived independence."}]}, {"id": "f7f0b159-1ad6-4555-b8bd-416bd9e78a4e", "type": "topic", "title": "Minimizing Harm and Covering Vulnerable Communities", "description": "Balances public need to know with compassion, trauma awareness, dignity, and proportionality.", "children": [{"id": "9e74ccfa-aabe-47aa-87ff-3657cea0a04d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Harm analysis", "children": [{"id": "9fc0b0b2-3e3a-4ce1-a14d-1c7640cb01d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Necessity"}, {"id": "c71196a0-1bcd-4f3a-b137-e81867106e0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportionality"}, {"id": "14ddcb47-00d7-4900-afc7-87a8d1463098", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternatives"}, {"id": "51696f6a-9031-48e0-8f41-535262f140fb", "type": "concept", "title": "After-publication impact"}], "description": "Students weigh public value against foreseeable harm to individuals and communities."}, {"id": "2e074553-d5fc-416e-959b-c1775c5802d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma-informed reporting", "children": [{"id": "45314671-46fe-49c5-898f-a73e42f3ed97", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent"}, {"id": "e242ed81-2f3d-4f0c-bbea-d88d4b3ac650", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview pacing"}, {"id": "16cf08fb-55c4-4272-9a97-0a8d1ce15365", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphic detail choices"}, {"id": "cad27127