 "concept", "title": "Social media reuse"}, {"id": "833b06e7-88ec-4500-81b3-196865ae2d19", "type": "concept", "title": "Revoked cooperation"}], "description": "Consent is complicated by power, vulnerability, age, trauma, and digital permanence."}, {"id": "ebea2f9d-a896-4749-838e-db264a1bb845", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital privacy", "children": [{"id": "fabb0a92-4d2f-415d-90cd-b49549758196", "type": "concept", "title": "Doxxing risk"}, {"id": "a38b3bdc-4c3e-4faa-9b44-6770638073e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive permanence"}, {"id": "333f3f8a-7173-4979-a752-1bb1f990aa27", "type": "concept", "title": "Searchability"}, {"id": "d5b74abf-f877-463e-9cc4-b376bef9c645", "type": "concept", "title": "Context collapse"}], "description": "Publicly available information can still create ethical risk when amplified."}]}, {"id": "41efd291-d142-445d-97c9-7494a2197031", "type": "topic", "title": "Deception, Undercover Reporting, and Hidden Methods", "description": "Tests the narrow circumstances under which deception or covert methods may be ethically defensible.", "children": [{"id": "46bd4366-928b-4f49-aeba-07ae5d89f1f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deception tests", "children": [{"id": "2f1980f5-c2ef-4b39-a24f-9629a72d4567", "type": "concept", "title": "No viable alternative"}, {"id": "70463c3d-6269-466f-933d-5554a1686849", "type": "concept", "title": "High public interest"}, {"id": "d2a478af-8bca-4935-993d-f161bf5d56df", "type": "concept", "title": "Limited deception"}, {"id": "10645a75-607b-41a9-b1f9-7b901ec3e4fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Editor oversight"}], "description": "Students learn why deception is rare and what standards must be met before considering it."}, {"id": "5f84030c-6388-471f-a29e-935e1d4c8735", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Undercover methods", "children": [{"id": "0e22aa22-7521-4d20-809b-83975e47b81d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hidden cameras"}, {"id": "c9f5fa41-a619-4bbb-9c62-87f09b1fa631", "type": "concept", "title": "Misrepresentation"}, {"id": "78efae84-dd23-4967-aee2-15d185339fc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety planning"}, {"id": "8ecc36b2-102d-4e6b-baca-c62b654d5c80", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosure to audience"}], "description": "Covert reporting requires planning, safety, legal awareness, and transparent post-publication explanation."}, {"id": "3a9c2a7d-253a-48d9-a36e-b0f7f8747c5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical alternatives", "children": [{"id": "186a6b19-a26a-4248-a079-efad1a28fed3", "type": "concept", "title": "Records"}, {"id": "6e395724-ffee-4bf2-a1d2-b50cefc4aa01", "type": "concept", "title": "Witnesses"}, {"id": "9b33ffdb-c32c-4f9e-9e1e-f4f61aa651e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Data"}, {"id": "fbe39c52-7fb0-4b29-92d0-0cd889e9dc37", "type": "concept", "title": "On-the-record confrontation"}], "description": "Most investigations can be strengthened through open reporting rather than hidden methods."}]}, {"id": "bd575e61-2872-4c2e-a85a-c91135e8597c", "type": "topic", "title": "Objectivity, Fairness, Transparency, and Point of View", "description": "Updates traditional objectivity debates with fairness, evidence, transparency, and intellectual honesty.", "children": [{"id": "900385e3-3e6c-4363-a4c7-dd904c5a257a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Objectivity debates", "children": [{"id": "23195dbd-4f07-48f5-93e1-8c7cf8f3fba5", "type": "concept", "title": "Method vs. neutrality"}, {"id": "5ece7c91-23eb-4bfa-b8f4-8686d1cbe104", "type": "concept", "title": "Both-sides problems"}, {"id": "5d0d8ecf-d45b-4863-b5de-99a9d53d54e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence hierarchy"}, {"id": "48409b66-7882-487c-ae38-5bff2483ddc2", "type": "concept", "title": "Observer bias"}], "description": "Students examine objectivity as method, aspiration, contested ideal, and newsroom norm."}, {"id": "e211a4fe-e81f-47ec-afe1-b2c7db803860", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fairness practice", "children": [{"id": "e7cb3470-2e9b-4e28-aaab-ef30ea10f476", "type": "concept", "title": "Right of reply"}, {"id": "345bc02b-701b-4a90-bc10-ae796b1d89b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportional sourcing"}, {"id": "1dc8e28b-d6c8-4299-8056-10520a09a39f", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding false balance"}, {"id": "aa144e54-2bea-4948-8296-269a7d736be4", "type": "concept", "title": "Contextual framing"}], "description": "Fairness means accurate representation of evidence, perspectives, and response opportunities."}, {"id": "1ecc42e7-399f-4289-84fd-887461ce0d82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transparency", "children": [{"id": "e74befa5-1eeb-4a67-98ff-c9007fc6a554", "type": "concept", "title": "How we know"}, {"id": "3d6dc4ab-f89c-4672-9b45-c5e41974edf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Method notes"}, {"id": "6186804b-82e7-4145-915f-1d205c08d9fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrections links"}, {"id": "abb4c103-2e94-43fa-a11a-fe26b3763aad", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporter disclosure"}], "description": "Students learn how explaining process can strengthen credibility without replacing verification."}]}, {"id": "5e572bde-60c0-4cfe-bbad-37e5415481ac", "type": "topic", "title": "Diversity, Representation, and Equity in Coverage", "description": "Builds ethical reporting habits around language, framing, stereotypes, power, and community context.", "children": [{"id": "d8075a56-cdbf-4b5c-9eb4-3299b96e90d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive sourcing", "children": [{"id": "bd0473ec-617a-4e35-b0e7-ffb67906f20e", "type": "concept", "title": "Source audits"}, {"id": "3f4a23d8-d80e-47e8-b47f-3f367643b0d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Community voices"}, {"id": "ce752138-e615-48e7-8ebc-ac8afb2451be", "type": "concept", "title": "Expert diversity"}, {"id": "ac4e6688-c7f6-4dd7-917c-4929497dbe38", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access"}], "description": "Coverage quality improves when source networks reflect affected communities and expertise."}, {"id": "9e597a23-e35e-4949-b856-bf1eabd167d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Framing and stereotypes", "children": 